N minus 2,", "tokens": [50864, 1804, 426, 3175, 568, 11, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 55, "seek": 13728, "start": 149.28, "end": 151.28, "text": " plus N minus 3.", "tokens": [50964, 1804, 426, 3175, 805, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 56, "seek": 13728, "start": 151.28, "end": 153.28, "text": " In this way, if I add 3, plus 2, plus 1,", "tokens": [51064, 682, 341, 636, 11, 498, 286, 909, 805, 11, 1804, 568, 11, 1804, 502, 11, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 57, "seek": 13728, "start": 153.28, "end": 155.28, "text": " to all of them.", "tokens": [51164, 281, 439, 295, 552, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 58, "seek": 13728, "start": 155.28, "end": 157.28, "text": " Can I say that I have an arithmetic progression here?", "tokens": [51264, 1664, 286, 584, 300, 286, 362, 364, 42973, 18733, 510, 30, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 59, "seek": 13728, "start": 157.28, "end": 159.28, "text": " Can I say it in reverse?", "tokens": [51364, 1664, 286, 584, 309, 294, 9943, 30, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 60, "seek": 13728, "start": 159.28, "end": 161.28, "text": " 1 plus 2, plus 3, plus 4.", "tokens": [51464, 502, 1804, 568, 11, 1804, 805, 11, 1804, 1017, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 61, "seek": 13728, "start": 161.28, "end": 163.28, "text": " And up to where? Up to N.", "tokens": [51564, 400, 493, 281, 689, 30, 5858, 281, 426, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 62, "seek": 13728, "start": 163.28, "end": 165.28, "text": " So what is its sum?", "tokens": [51664, 407, 437, 307, 1080, 2408, 30, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23024827080803947, "compression_ratio": 1.8773584905660377, "no_speech_prob": 0.05636104196310043}, {"id": 63, "seek": 16528, "start": 165.28, "end": 167.28, "text": " N plus 1 by 2.", "tokens": [50364, 426, 1804, 502, 538, 568, 13, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 64, "seek": 16528, "start": 167.28, "end": 168.28, "text": " What is this?", "tokens": [50464, 708, 307, 341, 30, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 65, "seek": 16528, "start": 168.28, "end": 170.28, "text": " N square plus N by 2.", "tokens": [50514, 426, 3732, 1804, 426, 538, 568, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 66, "seek": 16528, "start": 170.28, "end": 172.28, "text": " And I can say this", "tokens": [50614, 400, 286, 393, 584, 341, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 67, "seek": 16528, "start": 172.28, "end": 174.28, "text": " that it will be big of", "tokens": [50714, 300, 309, 486, 312, 955, 295, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 68, "seek": 16528, "start": 174.28, "end": 176.28, "text": " N square.", "tokens": [50814, 426, 3732, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 69, "seek": 16528, "start": 176.28, "end": 177.28, "text": " So when will be the worst case?", "tokens": [50914, 407, 562, 486, 312, 264, 5855, 1389, 30, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 70, "seek": 16528, "start": 177.28, "end": 178.28, "text": " The worst case will be", "tokens": [50964, 440, 5855, 1389, 486, 312, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 71, "seek": 16528, "start": 178.28, "end": 180.28, "text": " when in my ascending order,", "tokens": [51014, 562, 294, 452, 15526, 2029, 1668, 11, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 72, "seek": 16528, "start": 180.28, "end": 182.28, "text": " my pivot element is always the largest element.", "tokens": [51114, 452, 14538, 4478, 307, 1009, 264, 6443, 4478, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 73, "seek": 16528, "start": 182.28, "end": 183.28, "text": " In that case,", "tokens": [51214, 682, 300, 1389, 11, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 74, "seek": 16528, "start": 183.28, "end": 184.28, "text": " every single level will increase", "tokens": [51264, 633, 2167, 1496, 486, 3488, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 75, "seek": 16528, "start": 184.28, "end": 186.28, "text": " the time complexity.", "tokens": [51314, 264, 565, 14024, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 76, "seek": 16528, "start": 186.28, "end": 188.28, "text": " From which the final worst-case time complexity", "tokens": [51414, 3358, 597, 264, 2572, 5855, 12, 9765, 565, 14024, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 77, "seek": 16528, "start": 188.28, "end": 189.28, "text": " will be equal to N square.", "tokens": [51514, 486, 312, 2681, 281, 426, 3732, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 78, "seek": 16528, "start": 189.28, "end": 190.28, "text": " And in the same case,", "tokens": [51564, 400, 294, 264, 912, 1389, 11, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 79, "seek": 16528, "start": 190.28, "end": 192.28, "text": " if it is sorted in descending order,", "tokens": [51614, 498, 309, 307, 25462, 294, 40182, 1668, 11, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 80, "seek": 16528, "start": 192.28, "end": 194.28, "text": " i.e. if this area is in reverse,", "tokens": [51714, 741, 13, 68, 13, 498, 341, 1859, 307, 294, 9943, 11, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2702790561475252, "compression_ratio": 1.821011673151751, "no_speech_prob": 0.027759676799178123}, {"id": 81, "seek": 19428, "start": 194.28, "end": 196.28, "text": " then it is always the smallest element.", "tokens": [50364, 550, 309, 307, 1009, 264, 16998, 4478, 13, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 82, "seek": 19428, "start": 196.28, "end": 197.28, "text": " So in that case,", "tokens": [50464, 407, 294, 300, 1389, 11, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 83, "seek": 19428, "start": 197.28, "end": 199.28, "text": " the same N square time complexity goes.", "tokens": [50514, 264, 912, 426, 3732, 565, 14024, 1709, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 84, "seek": 19428, "start": 199.28, "end": 200.28, "text": " Now the question is", "tokens": [50614, 823, 264, 1168, 307, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 85, "seek": 19428, "start": 200.28, "end": 202.28, "text": " that the worst-case time complexity of Quixote", "tokens": [50664, 300, 264, 5855, 12, 9765, 565, 14024, 295, 2326, 970, 1370, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 86, "seek": 19428, "start": 202.28, "end": 204.28, "text": " is asked in actual interviews.", "tokens": [50764, 307, 2351, 294, 3539, 12318, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 87, "seek": 19428, "start": 204.28, "end": 206.28, "text": " So you should already know this.", "tokens": [50864, 407, 291, 820, 1217, 458, 341, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 88, "seek": 19428, "start": 206.28, "end": 208.28, "text": " In fact, it is very important to remember this.", "tokens": [50964, 682, 1186, 11, 309, 307, 588, 1021, 281, 1604, 341, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 89, "seek": 19428, "start": 208.28, "end": 211.28, "text": " Make a note that the worst-case time complexity", "tokens": [51064, 4387, 257, 3637, 300, 264, 5855, 12, 9765, 565, 14024, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 90, "seek": 19428, "start": 211.28, "end": 214.28, "text": " comes into my Quixote when my pivot element", "tokens": [51214, 1487, 666, 452, 2326, 970, 1370, 562, 452, 14538, 4478, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 91, "seek": 19428, "start": 214.28, "end": 217.28, "text": " is always the smallest element", "tokens": [51364, 307, 1009, 264, 16998, 4478, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}, {"id": 92, "seek": 19428, "start": 217.28, "end": 220.28, "text": " or always the largest element.", "tokens": [51514, 420, 1009, 264, 6443, 4478, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2943227044467268, "compression_ratio": 1.9151785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 0.027104755863547325}], "language": "English"}